From 40edb9ae360ed74fb62e7a5895d2466226082358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] video-driver: iris33: reset the vcodec core on Eliza

__power_off_iris33_controller asserts the MVS0 (vcodec core) reset
only when the platform names one, and the Eliza table names none. The
vcodec core then keeps its state across power collapses, including
the output address of the capture buffer the firmware held when the
capture port stopped, and writes that buffer's last rows at the next
power-off and power-on, after the session closed and freed it:

  capture STOP acked 25189.6 ms, session closed 25190.7 ms
  power-off 26716.9 ms, pixel fault iova 0xdffce780 at 26721.3 ms
  power-on  45325.5 ms, pixel fault iova 0xdffce080 at 45329.2 ms

The next session hangs ("VCODEC HW is hung due to (CCE 1"). An
encoder's BIN buffer is also written after its release. Vendor parts
name video_mvs0_reset; the Eliza binding has no such reset, so nothing
failed until a stale write hit a freed buffer.

Use the vcodec0_core reset when the Eliza DT provides it. With it, 9
rounds of GStreamer and encode sessions each followed by a power
collapse or a rebind gave no fault and no hang; the one round run
without it, on the same build, faulted and hung. A DT without the
reset logs it and runs as before.

Fixes: 3368a86d51e9 ("video-driver: eliza: add platform support")
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [qualcomm-linux/video-driver]
---
 driver/platform/eliza/src/eliza.c           | 1 +
 driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/driver/platform/eliza/src/eliza.c b/driver/platform/eliza/src/eliza.c
index bd88bad2..842b34ea 100644
--- a/driver/platform/eliza/src/eliza.c
+++ b/driver/platform/eliza/src/eliza.c
@@ -1875,6 +1875,7 @@ static const struct clk_rst_table eliza_clk_reset_table[] = {
 	{ "bus",  0 },
 	{ "xo",   1 },
 	{ "core", 0 },
+	{ "vcodec0_core", 0, true },
 };
 
 /* name, start, size, secure, dma_coherant, region, dma_mask */
diff --git a/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c b/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c
index 903d76ac..7380255f 100644
--- a/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c
+++ b/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c
@@ -192,7 +192,6 @@ static const struct iris33_res_names iris33_res_vendor = {
 	.xo_rst    = "video_xo_reset",
 };
 
-/* qcom,eliza-iris: the binding has no MVS0 reset */
 static const struct iris33_res_names iris33_res_eliza = {
 	.axi_clk   = "iface",
 	.ctl_clk   = "core",
@@ -202,6 +201,7 @@ static const struct iris33_res_names iris33_res_eliza = {
 	.hw_gdsc   = "vcodec0",
 	.axi_rst   = "bus",
 	.ctl_rst   = "core",
+	.hw_rst    = "vcodec0_core",
 	.xo_rst    = "xo",
 };
 
